-- Source module: Solutions.KIL5Swap
/-!
# KIL5: the level-`0` interchange with run-time sizes, and the descriptor stacks

`prog C q 0 P L A B Cs` is the interchange of the two digits (fields of size `q`) of
`P :: L :: swShape A B Cs q`.  KIL3 realised it by `swapB`, two Lemma 3 field moves whose size
parameters are *literals*.  Here the size parameters are *expressions*, evaluated at run time:

* `withPush l p`: push the expressions `l`, run `p`, pop them (`Sp.withPush`);
* `swapE a q b c`: the two field moves with parameters read from expressions (`swapE_sp`):
  on `A0 ++ q :: (B ++ q :: Cs)` it computes the digit interchange when `a, q, b, c` evaluate to
  `vol A0, q, vol B, vol Cs`;
* the descriptor stacks `dJ … dT` (level, `P`, `L`, `vol A`, `vol B`, `vol Cs`, tower of moduli),
  `DescIn`, and `lev0U`, the uniform level-`0` code reading the descriptor (`lev0U_sp`).
